A||N||4||vipersyj||Is this the right Alternator Please help?||||1||
Z||000000||vipersyj||12-15-2001||07:50 PM||||The alternator I bought from NAPA has the heatshield and plug inlet mounted in a differant place.  WIth it still work I called and it is the correct part.  Also what is the best method to tighten belt when I get it in.  I have a 86 2.8 with a automatic. Can you tighten from bottom with auto.<P>Thanks<BR>Jesse||||reg||1
Z||000001||GTDude||12-15-2001||08:25 PM||||The heatshield is no problem.  The alternator is set to the wrong rotation even though it is the correct alternator.  Take it back and have them rotate it to the right place.  I was under the impression that the 88 model had a serpentine belt.  If this is true then it has a tensioner I believe and you should be able to put a wrench on the tensioner and either raise or lower it to take the tension off of it.  Then you can just slip the belt on.<BR>Oops, I see it's an 86.  Yes the 86 must be tightened from beneath....or it's easier anyway.  Good luck<BR>------------------<BR>GTDude's 86GT<p>[This message has been edited by GTDude (edited 12-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||SLYGUY||12-16-2001||12:24 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by GTDude:<BR><B>The alternator is set to the wrong rotation even though it is the correct alternator.  Take it back and have them rotate it to the right place.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>EXACT same thing happened to me. I had to replace my alternator in my 88GT. We compared my burnt alt. to the model that NAPA specifies (high amp) and mine was "clocked" wrong also. The rebuilt alternator had the wrong pulley on it also. Besides those two things, the two alternators were exactly the same. I hem and hawed about not wanting to buy a brand new one and he offered to swap pulleys and re-clock it. <P>Turned out great!!<P>Good luck<BR>Sly<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ViewImage.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Bugsy||12-17-2001||06:08 PM||||I've put 3 alternators in my '86 SE 2.8, and every one of them came with the wrong pulley.  Thank God for lifetime warranties  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>86 SE I'm addicted and proud of it<BR>Kevin||||reg||1
Z||000004||Formula88||12-17-2001||11:49 PM||||BTW, 88's do use a serpentine belt, but don't have a tensioner.  You adjust them like a conventional V-belt, but it uses the serpentine style.  I recommend Goodyear Gatorback belts, BTW.<P>I got the NAPA rebuilt 105 amp for mine about a month ago.  Worth the extra money.  Has a lifetime guarantee including towing if it ever fails.||||reg||1
